<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Geislingen an der Steige</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Geislingen an der Steige is a town in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/goppingen">Göppingen</a> district of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baden-wurttemberg">Baden-Württemberg</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, on the Fils where the road and railway from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stuttgart">Stuttgart</a> to Ulm climb the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swabian-jura">Swabian Jura</a> by the steep Geislinger Steige. It grew below the castle of the counts of Helfenstein, who sold it to the imperial city of Ulm in 1396. It passed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a> in 1803 and to Württemberg in 1810.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/geislingen-an-der-steige.jpg" alt="Geislingen an der Steige" width="320" height="260" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hagar66 based on work of TUBS · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Geislingen_an_der_Steige_in_GP.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
